preConditionHook:
// EQUAL HIGHS, THEN THE CLOSE THROUGH THEM (G06-23) -- Grimes's precise entry
// timing inside a pullback. The equalBarsCount bars ENDING ONE BAR AGO all
// share the same high to within toleranceTicks, and THIS bar closes above the
// highest of them. The short is the mirror: equal lows, and a close below them.
//
// KEPT WHOLE LIKE A CROSSING. The flat level and the close through it are one
// event, and no pane-AND reaches it: MicroDoubleExtreme states the
// matching-extremes half alone AND assigns the sides the other way round
// (matching LOWS on the long side, the micro double bottom), so an AND of that
// rule with a breakout would pair the wrong level with the wrong trigger.
// Ledge is the anchored multi-bar form of the same flat level and is likewise
// not the trigger.
//
// THE TOLERANCE STAYS IN TICKS, as MicroDoubleExtreme's does: Grimes means
// literally equal highs, and a tick count passes the shift test because a tick
// is a constant of the symbol, not a fraction of the price. THE TICK is EL's
// own MinMove / PriceScale, both VERIFIED and per-symbol constant for the whole
// run, written DIVISION-FIRST in both twins so the C++ reads token for token
// against its EasyLanguage (README "N ticks", TICKSIZE_FINDINGS.md).
//
// THE WINDOW ENDS ONE BAR AGO so the breakout bar's own high cannot be one of
// the equal highs it is breaking. At the default equalBarsCount 2 the test is
// fabs(high[1] - high[2]) <= toleranceTicks * tickSize and the level is the
// higher of those two bars.
//
// The equality is measured against high[1], the NEWEST bar of the run, so the
// run is a band of width toleranceTicks around that bar rather than a chain of
// pairwise comparisons that could drift.
//
// The level loop is Extremes()' seeded strict-comparison scan over the same
// shifted window; Extremes is EL SOURCE, so el_gt / el_lt carry the relational
// tolerance. AbsValue is ACCEPTED pure scalar arithmetic, std::fabs here.
//
// Written WITHOUT an early exit so the loop matches the EL twin statement for
// statement: EasyLanguage has no loop break, and the flag is cleared rather
// than the scan abandoned.
//
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope, so the hooks
// survive a double placement; every one is fully assigned each bar before it is
// read.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
eqHi = true;
eqLo = true;
lvlHi = high[1];
lvlLo = low[1];
for (int kk = 2; kk <= (int)equalBarsCount; ++kk) {
    if (el_gt(std::fabs(high[kk] - high[1]), toleranceTicks * tickSize)) eqHi = false;
    if (el_gt(std::fabs(low[kk] - low[1]), toleranceTicks * tickSize)) eqLo = false;
    if (el_gt(high[kk], lvlHi)) lvlHi = high[kk];
    if (el_lt(low[kk], lvlLo)) lvlLo = low[kk];
}
